          <p class="eyebrow">START WITH WHAT PEOPLE ARE ACTUALLY FEELING</p>
          <h2 class="hero-title hero-title-tight">Economic dignity for real life</h2>
          <p class="hero-subtitle hero-subtitle-wide">The monthly squeeze is where this starts.</p>
          <p class="hero-subtitle hero-subtitle-wide">
            Economy for Everyone starts with what people are actually feeling: the monthly squeeze.
            When the systems we rely on - housing, healthcare, childcare, education, transportation
            - get harder to afford and harder to navigate, trust thins, guardrails weaken, and it
            gets easier for distraction and division to replace problem-solving. E4E exists to push
            in the other direction: plain language, real receipts, and practical levers - so
            ordinary people can take small, steady actions that compound. The newer model is also
            explicit that some systems fail because capacity is too thin, and some fail because
            low-choice conditions make opacity and extraction profitable.
            <strong>Community is a verb, not a vibe.</strong>
          </p>
